  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1230 AM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nThe aforementioned upper level low to our southwest will\ncontinue trekking eastward south of the area today into\nWednesday morning. Guidance keeps any measurable\nprecipitation/all impacts away from the area, however it should \nbe noted that there's a chance (albeit very low - <10%) of some \ndrizzle over far southwest MO very early Wednesday morning \nbefore sunrise. Guidance isn't quite picking up on this yet \n(hence the very low probabilities), however saturated air (RH > \n85%) combined with upward omega, upslope flow, and a lack of \ncloud ice would suggest this to at least be possible. Again, \nit's a very localized area, with the better likelihood being all\nprecipitation remaining south of the CWA.\n\nThe warming trend continues through midweek, with highs in the\n70s on Tuesday and the 60s on Wednesday.\n\nAdditionally on Wednesday, an upper level shortwave trough will\npivot southeast through the Plains towards the region, with an\nassociated surface cold front progged to sweep through the area.\nGuidance now keeps any precipitation chances out of our area,\nas the better forcing lies east of Missouri over the\nOhio/Tennessee Valleys. The main impacts this system will bring\nto the area will be gusty winds up to 20-30mph (due to the tight\npressure gradient), and cooler air behind the front.\n\nThis will result in temperatures dropping a few degrees below\nnormal to finish out the week, with highs in the 50s on Thursday\nand the mid 40s to low 50s Friday. Friday night/Saturday morning\nwill be the chilliest night in the forecast period, with\novernight lows dropping into the low to mid 20s east of Highway\n65, and the upper 20s to low 30s west of the highway. \n\nThe next chance of precipitation will be towards the end of next\nweekend as another upper level shortwave pushes towards the\nregion. With it being so far out, current probabilities are only\n20-30%, however we'll continue monitoring how this system plays\nout this week to see if we can get a better idea on what to\nexpect.",
